changes.change:
Differential test over seeded random file-schema dbs: journal pages with and without :block/type "journal", pages without journal-day, markers NOW/DOING/TODO/LATER/DONE, tasks inside and outside the window. For each of these, assert (set (jw/run ...)) = (set (d/q ...)):
- built-in NOW and NEXT (with the task rule in % via add-rules-to-query);
- Johan's override, both raw and compat-rewritten;
- windows crossing a month boundary and a year boundary (20251225..20260108), and > vs >=.

Also assert ::no-match for near-miss shapes: an extra clause, a user-defined `task` rule, non-integer inputs, a find other than a single pull, or a missing bound. Add a perf smoke test: a db with 20k journal pages and 100k task blocks outside the window must answer in a few ms.
